# Provider auth for pi inside sandboxes — the .env passthrough contract.
#
# Copy this file to .env (gitignored) and set the credential variables your pi
# provider needs. EVERY variable in .env is injected as process env into every
# sandbox — names are not filtered, so any provider pi supports works with zero
# code changes. `./install` seeds .env from ~/.pi/agent/auth.json (one
# <provider-slug>_API_KEY per entry, values never printed).
#
# Examples — uncomment and fill in what your provider needs:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# XIAOMI_TOKEN_PLAN_SGP_API_KEY=
#
# No .env needed:
#   - exported *_API_KEY host vars (plus any names listed in PI_SANDBOX_EXTRA_ENV)
#     are forwarded to every sandbox exec by `pis`
#   - keyless providers (e.g. a local llama.cpp endpoint): PI_SANDBOX_ALLOW_NO_AUTH=1
